      "title": "‘I never executed Jesse Baird’: Beau Lamarre-Condon reenacts shooting when giving evidence in NSW trial",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/09/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-reenacts-shooting-jesse-baird-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Former police officer has pleaded not guilty to murdering Baird and Luke Davies in Paddington in early 2024</p><ul><li><p><em><strong>Warning: </strong>This article contains graphic content</em></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Beau Lamarre-Condon has told a Sydney court he did not “execute” Jesse Baird as he acted out the way he allegedly shot the 26-year-old.</p><p>The former police officer is accused of fatally shooting Baird and his new partner, Luke Davies, with his police service weapon in Baird’s Paddington home in Sydney on 19 February 2024.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/09/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-reenacts-shooting-jesse-baird-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
